//
// The OS oboec was built for, which is the OS it compiles for unless told
// otherwise. src/codegen.c gets this from the preprocessor; the Oboe spelling
// is a per-OS module file, which is the mechanism the language already has for
// exactly this. Resolution prefers hostos.<target>.oboe and falls back here,
// so this file is the `#else` arm -- and, as in the C, the BSDs land in it.
var HOST_OS = "linux"
